<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stephen of Perm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1340–1396</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Saint Stephen of Perm</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stephen of Perm was a Russian missionary monk from Ustyug who converted many of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/komi-peoples">Komi</a> people to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> from 1379 and became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Perm in 1383. He created the Old Permic alphabet for the Komi language and translated liturgical texts into it. He is venerated as a saint of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-orthodox-church">Russian Orthodox Church</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stephen-of-perm.jpg" alt="Stephen of Perm" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Лицевое житие преподобного Сергия Радонежского · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bishop_Stefan_of_Perm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
